### 1.2 Existing Pages
1. `index.html`: Landing page with hero, features, and floating chatbot widget.
2. `login.html`: Email/password login form.
3. `register.html`: Full name, email, password registration form.
4. `dashboard.html`: Student dashboard showing metric cards (Resume score 85%, Applied jobs count, AI interviews 7, progress 60%).
5. `profile.html`: Displays name, email, role, phone with inline edit for name/phone.
6. `resume.html`: Upload PDF form, status card, view resume button.
7. `jobs.html`: Jobs list, keyword search, type filter pills, mock apply modal.

### 1.3 Existing Backend Routes
- `POST /api/auth/register`: Create user account & issue JWT.
- `POST /api/auth/login`: Authenticate email/password & issue JWT.
- `GET /api/auth/me`: Get current logged-in user profile.
- `PUT /api/auth/profile`: Update basic profile fields (`fullName`, `phone`).
- `GET /api/jobs`: List all jobs (with auto-seeding if empty).
- `GET /api/jobs/:id`: Fetch single job.
- `POST /api/jobs`: Create job (requires token).
- `POST /api/resume/upload`: Upload PDF resume with Multer.
- `GET /api/resume/myresume`: Get uploaded resume metadata for logged-in student.
- `GET /uploads/:filename`: Static PDF file serving.

### 1.4 Existing Models
- `User`: `fullName`, `email`, `password`, `role` (student/company/admin), `phone`, `profileImage`.
- `Resume`: `userId`, `fileName`, `filePath`, `uploadedAt`.
- `Job`: `title`, `company`, `location`, `salary`, `type`, `experience`, `skills`, `description`, `applyUrl`.

### 1.5 Existing Controllers
- `authController.js`: Handles register, login, getMe, updateProfile.
- `jobController.js`: Handles getAllJobs, getJobById, createJob.
- Note: Resume logic is currently placed directly inside `resumeRoutes.js`.

### 1.6 Existing Middleware
- `authMiddleware.js`: `protect` verifies Bearer JWT token from Authorization header.

### 1.7 Existing Working Features
- User registration with bcrypt hashing and JWT generation.
- User login and authentication check.
- Basic profile viewing and name/phone update.
- Multer PDF resume upload and persistence in `backend/uploads/`.
- Job listing with search, category filtering, and fallback mock dataset when offline.
- Landing page with responsive styling and basic client-side chat widget.

### 1.8 Existing Broken Features & Bugs
- **Job Applications are completely fake**: In `js/jobs.js`, clicking "Apply Now" only stores job IDs in browser `localStorage`. There is no `Application` model, no database record, and no way for recruiters or admins to view applicants.
- **Saved Jobs is missing**: No database or UI feature for saving jobs for later.
- **Resume cleanup missing**: When a user uploads a new resume, the old physical PDF file is never deleted from `backend/uploads/`, causing orphan files and disk bloat.
- **Resume Download endpoint missing**: Resume only supports viewing directly via static URL; no dedicated download stream with proper `Content-Disposition`.
- **Resume Delete endpoint missing**: No way for a student to delete an existing resume.
- **Authorization missing**: Any authenticated user (including student) can send `POST /api/jobs` because there is no role authorization check (`authorize("company", "admin")`).
- **Student Dashboard displays static mock numbers**: "85% Resume Score", "7 AI Interviews", "60% Placement Progress" are hardcoded.
- **Student Profile is missing critical placement data**: Missing college, degree, branch, graduation year, CGPA, skills, projects, certifications, internships, GitHub, LinkedIn, portfolio, and dynamic profile completion calculation.
- **Recruiter/Company Module is completely absent**: No company registration/login, no company dashboard, no candidate review, no application status progression, no interview scheduling.
- **Admin/Placement Cell Module is completely absent**: No admin portal, no placement stats, no student/company management.
- **AI features are superficial**: The landing chatbot only uses basic `if/else` checks for 4 words ("hello", "job", "resume"). There is no real AI Assistant, no resume analyzer, no interview prep engine.
- **Notifications & Interviews are missing**: No models or routes for notifications or interview scheduling.
- **Express does not serve frontend root**: `backend/server.js` only serves `/uploads`. The frontend files must be opened via Live Server or `file://`, and all API URLs are hardcoded to `http://localhost:5000`.

### 1.9 Missing Features (Against Project Spec)
1. Complete Role-Based Access Control (`student`, `company`, `admin`).
2. Comprehensive Student Profile with dynamic completion percentage.
3. Production Resume System: Download, Delete, Replace with disk file cleanup, file existence validation, and secure access.
4. Real Application Management: Database persistence, applicant tracking, and status pipeline (`Applied` -> `Under Review` -> `Shortlisted` -> `Interview` -> `Selected` -> `Rejected`).
5. Saved Jobs feature (Bookmark & manage saved jobs).
6. Complete Company / Recruiter Portal: Company dashboard, job creation/editing/deletion, applicant list, resume viewing, status updates, interview scheduling.
7. Complete Placement Cell / Admin Portal: Analytics, student directory, company directory, placement statistics.
8. Integrated AI Assistant & Interview Prep: Technical, HR, Aptitude, Resume Improvement, and Career Guidance with Gemini API support + robust offline fallback knowledge engine.
9. AI Resume Analyzer: Skill detection, missing skills, match score, ATS formatting feedback.
10. Notification System: Live notifications for status changes, interview invites, new jobs.
11. Unified Express Serving: Express serves both API and static frontend seamlessly with adaptive API base URL.

