## 3. Step-by-Step Implementation Roadmap

### Phase 1: Audit, Architecture & Error Handling
- Create unified `backend/server.js` that serves the root frontend static files and `/uploads`.
- Ensure MongoDB Atlas connection handles offline/timeout gracefully without crashing.
- Add `js/api.js` with centralized `API_BASE` and response handlers.

### Phase 2: Authentication & Role-Based Authorization
- Enhance `models/User.js` with comprehensive profile fields.
- Update `backend/middleware/authMiddleware.js` to add `authorize(...roles)`.
- Update `register.html` / `register.js` to allow registering as Student or Company/Recruiter.
- Update `login.html` / `login.js` to redirect users to their appropriate dashboard:
  - Student -> `dashboard.html`
  - Company -> `company-dashboard.html`
  - Admin -> `admin-dashboard.html`
- Protect frontend pages from unauthorized role access.

### Phase 3: Student Profile & Dynamic Dashboard
- Upgrade `profile.html` and `js/profile.js` to support all academic and professional fields:
  - Full Name, Phone, College, Degree, Branch, Graduation Year, CGPA, Skills, Projects, Experience, GitHub, LinkedIn, Portfolio.
  - Implement dynamic profile completion percentage calculation (`(filledFields / totalFields) * 100`).
- Update `dashboard.html` and `js/dashboard.js` to display real dynamic data:
  - Real profile completion meter.
  - Real resume status and score.
  - Real applied jobs count and active application status badges.
  - Real upcoming interviews list.
  - Personalized recommended jobs based on the student's skills.

### Phase 4: Production Resume Management
- Refactor resume logic into `backend/controllers/resumeController.js`.
- Add routes:
  - `POST /api/resume/upload` (Multer, deletes previous physical file on replace).
  - `GET /api/resume/myresume` (Fetches metadata + file existence check).
  - `GET /api/resume/download` (Authenticated secure file download stream).
  - `DELETE /api/resume/delete` (Deletes DB record and removes physical PDF from `backend/uploads/`).
- Update `resume.html` and `js/resume.js` with View, Download, Delete, and Replace actions, validation, and real feedback.

### Phase 5: Complete Job System
- Enhance `models/Job.js` with `companyId`, `eligibility`, `branch`, `deadline`, `status` (`Active`/`Closed`), `applicantsCount`.
- Add search, filtering (by job type, location, experience), sorting (newest, highest salary), and company-specific endpoints.

### Phase 6: Real Applications & Saved Jobs
- Create `models/Application.js` and `models/SavedJob.js`.
- Create `backend/controllers/applicationController.js` and `backend/controllers/savedJobController.js`.
- Connect `jobs.html` modal to `POST /api/applications/apply`.
- Create `applications.html` & `js/applications.js` for students to track application status.
- Add "Save Job" (bookmark) button to job cards and dashboard.

### Phase 7: Company / Recruiter Module
- Create `company-dashboard.html` and `js/company-dashboard.js`.
- Features:
  - Recruiter stats (active jobs, total applicants, shortlisted, interviews scheduled).
  - Post new job modal/form.
  - Manage posted jobs (edit, close, delete).
  - View candidate applications with full profile details.
  - View and download candidate resumes.
  - Update candidate status (`Applied` -> `Under Review` -> `Shortlisted` -> `Interview` -> `Selected` -> `Rejected`).
  - Schedule interview with date, time, round, and meeting link.

### Phase 8: Placement Cell / Admin Module
- Create `admin-dashboard.html` and `js/admin-dashboard.js`.
- Features:
  - Placement metrics: Total students, total companies, total jobs, placement percentage, average CTC.
  - Student directory with placement status and filters.
  - Company directory.
  - Job approval / management.
  - Placement statistics and reports.

### Phase 9: Notifications & Interview Management
- Create `models/Notification.js` and `models/Interview.js`.
- Auto-trigger notifications when:
  - Student applies for a job -> Company gets notified.
  - Company updates status or schedules interview -> Student gets notified.
  - New job is posted -> Relevant students get notified.
- Implement live notification dropdown/modal in top navigation bar across all pages.
- Student interview schedule section on dashboard and dedicated interview cards.

### Phase 10 & 11: AI Assistant & AI Resume Analyzer
- Build `backend/services/aiService.js`:
  - Connects to Google Gemini API (if `GEMINI_API_KEY` is present in `.env`).
  - Implements an intelligent, domain-specific placement & interview offline engine (never faking, clearly operating in offline/local AI mode with hundreds of curated technical/HR questions, coding tips, and ATS resume scoring).
- Build `backend/controllers/aiController.js` and `backend/routes/aiRoutes.js`:
  - `POST /api/ai/chat`: Interactive conversational assistant for placement prep, DSA, HR interview, and resume tips.
  - `POST /api/ai/interview-prep`: Role-specific interview questions generator (Frontend, Backend, Full Stack, Data Analyst, Cloud).
  - `POST /api/ai/analyze-resume`: Extracts skills, calculates ATS readiness score (0-100%), identifies missing keywords, and gives actionable improvements.
- Create `ai-assistant.html` & `js/ai-assistant.js` + link floating widget on `index.html`.

### Phase 12 & 13: Analytics, Reports & Security Audit
- Add placement analytics graphs / progress bars on Admin and Recruiter dashboards.
- Security verification:
  - JWT secret validation.
  - Password hashing with bcrypt.
  - Role-based route authorization.
  - PDF file extension, mime-type, and size limits (max 5MB).
  - Sanitization of user input.
  - Cross-user file access prevention.

### Phase 14 & 15: Responsive UI Polish & Comprehensive Testing
- Polish UI across all pages using the primary blue palette (`#2563EB`, `#1E40AF`, `#10B981`, `#F8FAFC`).
- Ensure mobile responsiveness for sidebar, topbar, grids, and modals.
- End-to-end testing of every role:
  - Student registration, profile completion, resume upload/download/delete, job search, save, apply, AI chat.
  - Recruiter registration, job posting, applicant review, status change, interview scheduling.
  - Admin login, metrics review, user management.

### Phase 16: Deployment Preparation & Presentation Support
- Document complete API endpoints in `README.md`.
- Provide clear setup and demo guide for college presentation.

